        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: consolidate reconnect supervisors",
        "body": "Related: #105907\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nGateway, channel, transcription, tunnel, and delivery-recovery reconnect paths each maintained their own attempt counting, backoff, cancellation, and exhaustion mechanics. That duplication made retry behavior easier to drift while guarding live connectivity.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a dependency-light `RetrySupervisor` beside the canonical backoff and abort-aware sleep primitives, then migrates each reconnect/restart path to it while leaving its protocol and domain state machine intact. Exact delivery-recovery schedules, Retry-After floors, stable-run resets, and site-specific max-attempt policies remain unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. Reconnect timing, retry limits, abort handling, handshake fallback, and channel restart policy stay the same, with one canonical supervision path for future fixes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcvgzn8hhbj50qjpxbrb1re` on final head: 448 focused tests passed across seven shards; scoped `oxfmt` and `oxlint` passed with 0 warnings/errors.\n- The same final-head Testbox passed `tsgo:core:all`, `tsgo:test:src`, `tsgo:test:packages`, `tsgo:prod`, `tsgo:scripts`, `tsgo:test:root`, and both extension package-boundary checks. Hosted CI `build-artifacts` also passed on the exact head.\n- Fresh autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Non-test diff: 204 additions, 205 deletions (net -1 LOC).\n- Broad gates retain unrelated current-main failures: the TypeScript LOC ratchet and the unchanged `extensions/qa-lab/src/suite.test.ts` mock missing newly required fields. No touched file is implicated.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n",
